#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0137 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
# Rule:Description: CRITyFL is populated and CRITy is not populated
#note "crit1fl=Y populated, crit1 empty, both spelled in lower case. Column names match case-insensitively on every surface (owner ruling 2026-09-28), so the lowercase spelling a SAS dataset may carry satisfies the Requirements.Variables.All templates and the rule executes with the same verdict as on the uppercase twin (CDISC-AD0137-invalid): CR137 — CRITy must be populated where CRITyFL is (ADaMIG 1.3 Table 3.3.4.2) -> violation."
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=01-701-1015
dataset ADLBC class=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col crit1fl type=Char
col crit1 type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALB | Y |
---
